#
# User-level override of the packaged LibreOffice desktop entry.
# (Comment lines are ignored by the Desktop Entry parser, so this header block
# is inert; the file has exactly one [Desktop Entry] group below.)
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
#
# The packaged entry runs `libreoffice` with no environment pinning, so
# LibreOffice auto-detects its VCL (widget toolkit) backend. On this machine
# qt6-base is installed, and that lands on the Qt6/KF6 backend, which the
# ArchWiki flags for visible scroll lag on Wayland:
#
#   "When on Wayland with the VCL interface set to qt6, it can result in lag
#    spikes when scrolling quickly. Setting the environment variables to gtk3
#    seems to be mostly stable."
#
# The GTK3 backend is also the one that honours the system GTK theme
# (Dracula) and the Papirus-Dark icon theme, so LibreOffice matches the rest
# of the desktop. The GTK4 backend is still experimental upstream.
#
# WHY THIS POINTS AT THE WRAPPER
#
# ~/.config/environment.d/70-libreoffice.conf carries the same setting, but
# that file is read once by the systemd-environment-d-generator at session
# start. A desktop file Exec= line does not go through the generator, and
# neither do `hyprctl dispatch exec` or a bare `env` call, so those paths
# would silently fall back to auto-detection.
#
# The wrapper (~/.local/bin/libreoffice) applies the pin on every launch
# path, and it is also where the headless profile isolation lives, so the
# desktop entries and the wrapper cannot drift apart.
#
# The first Exec token is deliberately the wrapper path and not "env": the
# launcher indexes an entry by the basename of that token (execBasename in
# quickshell Launcher.qml), so an Exec line starting with "env" would make
# this entry searchable as "env" rather than "libreoffice".
#
# MAINTENANCE: generated from the packaged entry. After a LibreOffice update,
# re-run the generator; only the Exec lines are intentional changes.

#
# This file is part of the LibreOffice project.
#
# This Source Code Form is subject to the terms of the Mozilla Public
# License, v. 2.0. If a copy of the MPL was not distributed with this
# file, You can obtain one at http://mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/.
#
# This file incorporates work covered by the following license notice:
